From da777eb31ca368796e05b7c1c17633e82ac470cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BiasClear <noreply@biasclear.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:45:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Explain spend: pause and debt never share a transaction
 with a contended item (306 fix b)

persistBillingPause wrote billing#pause and the event's debt in one
transaction. Every reserve ConditionChecks billing#pause, so under
DynamoDB's conflict rule an ordinary concurrent reserve cancelled it and
both records were lost; two unresolved events lost the second debt.

- The event's debt row (a key nothing else writes) is written first, then
  the shared pause, each as its own PutItem overwrite, retried up to 4
  times with jitter and read back before each retry. No counter is
  touched, so a retry can't double-count.
- A bound breach's settlement commits its own debt row with the event and
  counters instead of the shared pause; the pause is then written alone
  and pausePersisted reports whether it landed (it was claimed before).
- New Ddb.put for overwrite-safe records.

Regressions (test/contention.test.ts, with test/conflicts.ts modelling
the conflict rule, adapted from the 306 harness): pause and debt while a
reserve holds the pause; an unknown-usage call during another reserve
still fences a fresh instance; two unresolved events keep both debts; a
breach settlement never touches billing#pause; a breach whose pause
can't be written reports pausePersisted=false and keeps its debt. The
first four fail on 19eebb3's spend code; dropping the retries or
claiming the pause fails them too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
